      ":question/id": "71350d61-9672-52ac-9492-4bd38fc59f6d",
      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-99063",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is the graph of $y=\\frac{4}{x}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To plot $y=\\frac{4}{x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](images/b3/b3a79a8dbe82342c0ab1e16371f8c1d82833f4ebc3bad659f1a619ab1e92733e.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $4$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{4}{x}.$\n\n![](images/e1/e10be40920aebaaf2f5984e25cff2143ee145851d5feaef48df883cf3556cacc.png)"
